It took too long for you to see that this was all part of it. Their trust comes not from your successes, but what they saw in you. They want to believe that any man can recover from this. They know Batman will, but they want to see someone like Bruce Wayne do it.

Your mind drifts as you raise your voice. The person wasn’t here, only the persona. You spoke loud, with energy. You had already given this speech a hundred times to an empty room. Now, a full room stared at an empty pulpit. They seemed to like the words, the sounds, and the intonations you gave. You saw their eyes beaming, some clapping. Can they see that the mirror is empty?



